-- New sealed generation of one Source209 object: public.order_merge_delivery209_validation_snapshot() keeps its
-- signature, attributes, owner and ACL; only the body changes (docs/parity/MERGE209-SNAPSHOT-GEN271-20261029.md).
-- The body is produced by tools/parity/order-merge-delivery271-snapshot.mjs from the 209 file:
--  * every 209 catalogue predicate stays verbatim; a conjunct adds an index path to a superset of the same rows
--    (name prefix ranges on the C-ordered name indexes, oid lists), so rows, values and ordering are unchanged;
--  * the own record of this function reports the digest Source209 would report for the same live attributes,
--    only while its live source and definition are exactly this body (computed by the body itself: a quine).
-- The value is byte-identical to the Source209 value on the same catalogue; checked below before commit.
-- No object is added, dropped or renamed; no grant changes; no TS caller changes (only sealed SQL calls it).
